                                        "entry_id": "062f2a4c-0f1f-36b8-901e-6cc3a12eee18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of blood or other liquid, to dry out and become hard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4a1705a-2750-4a4a-820e-440b1ab5d95b",
                                                "sense_id": "4b0c69e8-8e97-3c6d-b2b1-4bb3f330251b",
                                                "text": "Once we fell asleep, and, I think, must have slept for some hours, for, when we woke, our limbs were quite stiff, and the blood from our blows and scratches had caked, and was hard and dry upon our skin."
